(2132143, 287277, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b> You are really lucky to have got this setup but I feel you did not took full advantage of the shot which was offered. Overall a nice picture but there are distracting elements also.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> The edges look little softer but the image seems to be well exposed.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> This certainly is BLUE ...so it fits the challenge perfectly.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> This is an average composition. I think different angle might have helped. Again some basic stuff needs to be taken care of. Image is bit flat and it needs work on contrast. Some overall sharpening is needed. The gate seems to be distracting and different crop or angle would help. But yes- the red of tail-light is complimenting the blue and makes the blue stant out. Relflection look great.<br/> <br/>I did not voted for this challenge but would have given anything between 5-6 for this one. I must admit that you have got eye for interesting stuff :)<br/> <br/>You have got much better pictures in your profile ..and offcourse- a cool bike. Looking forward to more picture from you.<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic: You are really lucky to have got this setup but I feel you did not took full advantage of the shot which was offered. Overall a nice picture but there are distracting elements also. Technical: The edges look little softer but the image seems to be well exposed. Challenge: This certainly is BLUE ...so it fits the challenge perfectly. Conclusion: This is an average composition. I think different angle might have helped. Again some basic stuff needs to be taken care of. Image is bit flat and it needs work on contrast. Some overall sharpening is needed. The gate seems to be distracting and different crop or angle would help. But yes- the red of tail-light is complimenting the blue and makes the blue stant out. Relflection look great. I did not voted for this challenge but would have given anything between 5-6 for this one. I must admit that you have got eye for interesting stuff :) You have got much better pictures in your profile ..and offcourse- a cool bike. Looking forward to more picture from you. I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 01:25:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132191, 288649, 44924, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Rikki, you are on a roll my friend. This is your best picture yet, awesome capture.</td>', 'Congratulations Rikki, you are on a roll my friend. This is your best picture yet, awesome capture.', '2006-02-08 01:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132217, 286661, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/>Congratulation on such good score. The Image deserved it.<br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b> This one looks cool. Even though there are so many of this kind on DPC, this one stands out. <br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> Perfect. Well exposed and "appropriate" DOF. The focus is sharp and lighting is just right. How did you achieved such smooth texture of water...?<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> Not just fits the challenge but is amongst the best. No more comments on this one :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> Overall a great composition. Even though this is cliche shot, still you made it stand out from rest in the lot. I''m surely going to try this on my own. As many other comments hint- this does not even look real (though we know it is) and I really like it falling between two worlds. Looking forward to more submissions from you.<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Congratulation on such good score. The Image deserved it. Aesthetic: This one looks cool. Even though there are so many of this kind on DPC, this one stands out.  Technical: Perfect. Well exposed and "appropriate" DOF. The focus is sharp and lighting is just right. How did you achieved such smooth texture of water...? Challenge: Not just fits the challenge but is amongst the best. No more comments on this one :) Conclusion: Overall a great composition. Even though this is cliche shot, still you made it stand out from rest in the lot. I''m surely going to try this on my own. As many other comments hint- this does not even look real (though we know it is) and I really like it falling between two worlds. Looking forward to more submissions from you. I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 01:45:42.000000', NULL, 0),
