(2132277, 288542, 37818, '<td valign="top">Another great shot, Doc, I love the gentle tone of it. And an absolutely beautiful little girl! Congratulations :)</td>', 'Another great shot, Doc, I love the gentle tone of it. And an absolutely beautiful little girl! Congratulations :)', '2006-02-08 02:08:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132282, 288649, 10858, '<td valign="top">Way to go Rikki, this one was among my favourites! Are you going for the 50 ribbons instead of 5 this year? ;-) I am very curious how you did the fractal-like lemon drops, if you could write a short description, I would be very thankful. Pretty please.</td>', 'Way to go Rikki, this one was among my favourites! Are you going for the 50 ribbons instead of 5 this year? ;-) I am very curious how you did the fractal-like lemon drops, if you could write a short description, I would be very thankful. Pretty please.', '2006-02-08 02:12:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132298, 288649, 47020, '<td valign="top">exquisite shot!  congratulations!<br/> <br/>Enquiring minds do want to know, though, to borrow the phrasing of a previous poster: "what are the orbs?"<br/> <br/>????  I must know!  :-)<br/> <br/>Again, congrats.  A very worthy image.</td>', 'exquisite shot!  congratulations! Enquiring minds do want to know, though, to borrow the phrasing of a previous poster: "what are the orbs?" ????  I must know!  :-) Again, congrats.  A very worthy image.', '2006-02-08 02:18:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132308, 288426, 47020, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sumeetpuri:</b></div><hr/><i> how can you say its a baby blue?? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, why should I not?  It''s a baby''s eye (the kid in question is 6 months old), and it''s blue.<br/> <br/>I tinted the overall image towards blue a tad, too, which may have been a mistake, I don''t know... some have commented that they didn''t like the skin tones.<br/> <br/>*shrug*, live and learn, I guess.  :-)<br/> <br/>I did have some closer shots of her eye, and that had been the intention originally, but I thought this shot captured a double ententre, as she looks a little "blue" (as in sad) there, to me -- though I don''t think she actually was.<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks to those who left feedback.  Thanks even more to/if anybody''s reading this.  ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by sumeetpuri: how can you say its a baby blue??   Well, why should I not?  It''s a baby''s eye (the kid in question is 6 months old), and it''s blue. I tinted the overall image towards blue a tad, too, which may have been a mistake, I don''t know... some have commented that they didn''t like the skin tones. *shrug*, live and learn, I guess.  :-) I did have some closer shots of her eye, and that had been the intention originally, but I thought this shot captured a double ententre, as she looks a little "blue" (as in sad) there, to me -- though I don''t think she actually was. Anyway, thanks to those who left feedback.  Thanks even more to/if anybody''s reading this.  ;-)', '2006-02-08 02:21:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132315, 288245, 10858, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for all your great comments and words, I appreciate it very much! <br/> <br/>Agenkin, I thought a lot about yours and I have to agree both on the shadow, which I did not realize during the set up and the flip as well. Most people use their right hands, I missed a point here with the composition. <br/> <br/>I also would like to improve sharpness and quality, however noone mentioned it yet, I feel these two points might have been the weakness.</td>', 'Thank you all for all your great comments and words, I appreciate it very much!  Agenkin, I thought a lot about yours and I have to agree both on the shadow, which I did not realize during the set up and the flip as well. Most people use their right hands, I missed a point here with the composition.  I also would like to improve sharpness and quality, however noone mentioned it yet, I feel these two points might have been the weakness.', '2006-02-08 02:23:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132326, 288085, 43156, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Andrey, I think its an excellent finish.</td>', 'Congratulations Andrey, I think its an excellent finish.', '2006-02-08 02:29:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132328, 286720, 31403, '<td valign="top">202!!!  You were robbed - this photo has great simplicity about it that I think is neat.  Bright, shiny, noiseless images are the rage here at DPC, but this is a gem.<br/> <br/>Keep thinking, keep shooting, and don''t mind being different.  We need your creative input in our community.</td>', '202!!!  You were robbed - this photo has great simplicity about it that I think is neat.  Bright, shiny, noiseless images are the rage here at DPC, but this is a gem. Keep thinking, keep shooting, and don''t mind being different.  We need your creative input in our community.', '2006-02-08 02:30:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132368, 288649, 43156, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, amazing picture.<br/></td>', 'Congratulations, amazing picture.', '2006-02-08 02:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132402, 289352, 17126, '<td valign="top">You know what? I actually dig this picture. Very abstract. I think I see a tree in the background possibly, but that''s beside the point. it''s as if the focus is outside this window on a bright, rainy morning, but it''s so bright out, your can''t see anything. The contrast takes all the recognizable objects away, and you''re left with this nonobjective piece of art.<br/> <br/>I actually like it a lot. Please don''t let the score discourage you... You should see my first few entries! In fact, go look at them for real. Mine weren''t even good photos.<br/> <br/>Stick with DPC. You''ll develop a style, and you''ll learn from the comments you receive. Not from all of them, but by some of them for sure.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting!</td>', 'You know what? I actually dig this picture. Very abstract. I think I see a tree in the background possibly, but that''s beside the point. it''s as if the focus is outside this window on a bright, rainy morning, but it''s so bright out, your can''t see anything. The contrast takes all the recognizable objects away, and you''re left with this nonobjective piece of art. I actually like it a lot. Please don''t let the score discourage you... You should see my first few entries! In fact, go look at them for real. Mine weren''t even good photos. Stick with DPC. You''ll develop a style, and you''ll learn from the comments you receive. Not from all of them, but by some of them for sure. Keep shooting!', '2006-02-08 02:53:07.000000', NULL, 0),
