(2139037, 288841, 52296, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much for your voting, I''m very proud of my 7th place!!</td>', 'Thank you all very much for your voting, I''m very proud of my 7th place!!', '2006-02-10 01:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2139378, 288649, 52296, '<td valign="top">Congratulatoin Rikki, well done and deserved!!</td>', 'Congratulatoin Rikki, well done and deserved!!', '2006-02-10 06:24:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2140007, 287635, 40718, '<td valign="top">It was a difficult object to shoot, I''m sure, with the dynamic range of the darks and lights.  The highlight is a bit blown, which may have been impossible to help.  Otherwise the composition and technicals are good.  Perhaps the biggest thing is merely the subject.  I think there were too many shots of blue knick-knacks.  You will notice you had a huge spike of 5 votes.  I think people recognized the technical excellence, but just couldn''t get excited about the picture.</td>', 'It was a difficult object to shoot, I''m sure, with the dynamic range of the darks and lights.  The highlight is a bit blown, which may have been impossible to help.  Otherwise the composition and technicals are good.  Perhaps the biggest thing is merely the subject.  I think there were too many shots of blue knick-knacks.  You will notice you had a huge spike of 5 votes.  I think people recognized the technical excellence, but just couldn''t get excited about the picture.', '2006-02-10 11:17:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2140022, 288245, 40718, '<td valign="top">I like the technicals which are well done.  The composition is pretty good, although I may have cropped a bit more space into the left side (not a lot though).  The picture is fairly noisy along the gradient, which is odd for ISO 100.  People on DPC almost uniformly hate noise.  Perhaps a run through Neat Image would have cleared that up.  Like the last photo I commented on, I think the voters were rewarding your technicals with fewer really low scores, but perhaps couldn''t get excited enough about an empty jug to score it much higher.</td>', 'I like the technicals which are well done.  The composition is pretty good, although I may have cropped a bit more space into the left side (not a lot though).  The picture is fairly noisy along the gradient, which is odd for ISO 100.  People on DPC almost uniformly hate noise.  Perhaps a run through Neat Image would have cleared that up.  Like the last photo I commented on, I think the voters were rewarding your technicals with fewer really low scores, but perhaps couldn''t get excited enough about an empty jug to score it much higher.', '2006-02-10 11:21:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2140083, 289370, 40718, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 when I voted, but did notice a few things.  One, the highlight is saturated and appears to have suffered for it with some pixelation.  Two, the lime doesn''t look good in either the blue light or your PP color shift.  I wonder if you could have lit it with a small penlight or something to give it some more natural color.  Technicals are good, but a personal rule of mine is that anything with writing on it needs to be either sharply in focus or completely out of focus.  Partially focused letters are a no-no.  The eye hates that.  If you shot on a tripod, I would have gone with more than f1.8.</td>', 'I gave this a 6 when I voted, but did notice a few things.  One, the highlight is saturated and appears to have suffered for it with some pixelation.  Two, the lime doesn''t look good in either the blue light or your PP color shift.  I wonder if you could have lit it with a small penlight or something to give it some more natural color.  Technicals are good, but a personal rule of mine is that anything with writing on it needs to be either sharply in focus or completely out of focus.  Partially focused letters are a no-no.  The eye hates that.  If you shot on a tripod, I would have gone with more than f1.8.', '2006-02-10 11:35:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2140101, 286157, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, apparently we know you are capable of great work.  Darn you for bumping me to 4th in shadow.  Anyway, I gave this shot a 5.  A few limiting factors.  1) in "product ads" I think the subject should be fully in focus.  The top of the absolut bottle is soft.  If this was handheld, it could have been a bit of motion blur at 1/30th.  If it was on a tripod, then I would have bumped to at least f8.  2) The back rim of the glass is almost lost.  I think this lends confusion to the eye.  I actually can''t even tell if the glass contains something or not.  3) This is small, but the perspective seems to abnormally squash the bottle.<br/> <br/>I do like the gradient.  I''m guessing, although I could be wrong, that the blue was added mainly through PP and not through lighting.  I didn''t find these shots as appealing as something with natural light but a blue subject.  Having at least some true white in the shot was more pleasing to the eye.</td>', 'Well, apparently we know you are capable of great work.  Darn you for bumping me to 4th in shadow.  Anyway, I gave this shot a 5.  A few limiting factors.  1) in "product ads" I think the subject should be fully in focus.  The top of the absolut bottle is soft.  If this was handheld, it could have been a bit of motion blur at 1/30th.  If it was on a tripod, then I would have bumped to at least f8.  2) The back rim of the glass is almost lost.  I think this lends confusion to the eye.  I actually can''t even tell if the glass contains something or not.  3) This is small, but the perspective seems to abnormally squash the bottle. I do like the gradient.  I''m guessing, although I could be wrong, that the blue was added mainly through PP and not through lighting.  I didn''t find these shots as appealing as something with natural light but a blue subject.  Having at least some true white in the shot was more pleasing to the eye.', '2006-02-10 11:42:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2140423, 287809, 2223, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful!</td>', 'Very beautiful!', '2006-02-10 14:10:37.000000', NULL, 0),
