(2371520, 289162, 51125, '<td valign="top">I really like the design elements of this shot and the use of color to hold it together.  The two tone hair is unforunate but not much you could so about that.  I also would consider some adjustments to bring out the skin tone but you are pretty limited in basic editing.</td>', 'I really like the design elements of this shot and the use of color to hold it together.  The two tone hair is unforunate but not much you could so about that.  I also would consider some adjustments to bring out the skin tone but you are pretty limited in basic editing.', '2006-05-02 08:31:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2372177, 286642, 50674, '<td valign="top">I really do like your birdshots, and as you have probably seen, I like shoting them myself (only using a Nikon). And then there is this boatshed. I love this blue colour and the simplicity of the compostition, really works very well.<br/>It seems so perfect, but isn''t. There is that one woodboard that is askew and I know that most people would have cropped a little bit more at the bottom, but you didn''t and it makes for a little opening, a glimpse of the inside in a way.<br/>This was my very first challenge, Blue II, and I too picked a building. Didn''t do very well though.</td>', 'I really do like your birdshots, and as you have probably seen, I like shoting them myself (only using a Nikon). And then there is this boatshed. I love this blue colour and the simplicity of the compostition, really works very well.It seems so perfect, but isn''t. There is that one woodboard that is askew and I know that most people would have cropped a little bit more at the bottom, but you didn''t and it makes for a little opening, a glimpse of the inside in a way.This was my very first challenge, Blue II, and I too picked a building. Didn''t do very well though.', '2006-05-02 12:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2378587, 289313, 31133, '<td valign="top">Oh no! You have an entry without a single comment?! Here''s one from me - hope you don''t take offense, but know that it is meant with the best intentions, even if I am no dazzling photographer myself:-)<br/> <br/>I think the subject is so simple and straightforward that it has potential. Would probably be really fun to experiment with different lighting and composition with the same setup. It''s also the perfect kind of composition to practice post-processing skills with. I didn''t vote on this image, but if I had, I might have given it a 4 or a 5, and probably towards the 4 side. The lighting is a bit harsh and that really takes my attention away from whatever the subject is (the rings in this case). The repetitive idea is good. Still, I think that for the repetition to appeal to me (I can only speak for myself), it would have to be more. Alternatively, just one ring on a white background could be worth considering. But four rings is not enough to give me a defining pattern, nor is it few enough to give me a place to rest my poor old eyes. If the line of rings were at a diagonal, I think it could also add interest. <br/> <br/>Whew. This is one of my longest comments ever. Hope you don''t mind the rambling! Please PM me if what I say doesn''t make sense, or even if you would like me to ramble some more :-)</td>', 'Oh no! You have an entry without a single comment?! Here''s one from me - hope you don''t take offense, but know that it is meant with the best intentions, even if I am no dazzling photographer myself:-) I think the subject is so simple and straightforward that it has potential. Would probably be really fun to experiment with different lighting and composition with the same setup. It''s also the perfect kind of composition to practice post-processing skills with. I didn''t vote on this image, but if I had, I might have given it a 4 or a 5, and probably towards the 4 side. The lighting is a bit harsh and that really takes my attention away from whatever the subject is (the rings in this case). The repetitive idea is good. Still, I think that for the repetition to appeal to me (I can only speak for myself), it would have to be more. Alternatively, just one ring on a white background could be worth considering. But four rings is not enough to give me a defining pattern, nor is it few enough to give me a place to rest my poor old eyes. If the line of rings were at a diagonal, I think it could also add interest.  Whew. This is one of my longest comments ever. Hope you don''t mind the rambling! Please PM me if what I say doesn''t make sense, or even if you would like me to ramble some more :-)', '2006-05-03 18:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394861, 289398, 48928, '<td valign="top">This is so well done, i love it.  Great shot.</td>', 'This is so well done, i love it.  Great shot.', '2006-05-08 20:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2403276, 288086, 19311, '<td valign="top">There are a couple of things that would have helped this image.  First it would be nice if the blue extended all the way to the bottom of the frame.  The glasses could stand to be in sharper focus.  And finally, I think the shades of blue are a little to close to one another.  It would have made the image much more contrasty with a slightly wider range of the three shades.  All that being said, you still did fairly well in the challenge and with a little tweaking this could go from a good image to a great one.</td>', 'There are a couple of things that would have helped this image.  First it would be nice if the blue extended all the way to the bottom of the frame.  The glasses could stand to be in sharper focus.  And finally, I think the shades of blue are a little to close to one another.  It would have made the image much more contrasty with a slightly wider range of the three shades.  All that being said, you still did fairly well in the challenge and with a little tweaking this could go from a good image to a great one.', '2006-05-10 19:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2409404, 285838, 48739, '<td valign="top">I like this alot it looks really cool.... The water does look a little like silver or some sort of metal... I think if i was voting in the challenge i would of giving this a 8.</td>', 'I like this alot it looks really cool.... The water does look a little like silver or some sort of metal... I think if i was voting in the challenge i would of giving this a 8.', '2006-05-12 13:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
